                <li><button type="button" aria-describedby="pipeline-step-5" disabled><small>05</small><span>Phase</span></button></li>
                <li><button type="button" aria-describedby="pipeline-step-6" disabled><small>06</small><span>Review</span></button></li>
              </ol>
              <div class="pipeline-details">
                <div class="pipeline-detail" id="pipeline-step-1"><p><strong>Frame capture.</strong> Surgical video runs at 25 frames a second or more, so a live system has at most 40 ms per frame. Each frame reaches the model as a grid of pixel values.</p><div class="pipeline-models"><span>Example tools</span><ul><li>FFmpeg</li><li>OpenCV</li></ul></div></div>
                <div class="pipeline-detail" id="pipeline-step-2"><p><strong>Feature extraction.</strong> A backbone network turns each patch of the frame into a feature vector, a list of numbers that describes what the patch shows.</p><div class="pipeline-models"><span>Example models</span><ul><li>ResNet</li><li>Vision Transformer</li><li>DINOv2</li></ul></div></div>
                <div class="pipeline-detail is-active" id="pipeline-step-3"><p><strong>Segmentation.</strong> A segmentation model assigns every pixel a class, such as instrument, tissue, or background, which outlines each region.</p><div class="pipeline-models"><span>Example models</span><ul><li>U-Net</li><li>Mask R-CNN</li><li>SAM</li></ul></div></div>
                <div class="pipeline-detail" id="pipeline-step-4"><p><strong>Detection and tracking.</strong> A detector boxes each instrument, and a tracker links the boxes across frames, so each tool keeps its ID and its tip leaves a path.</p><div class="pipeline-models"><span>Example models</span><ul><li>YOLO</li><li>DETR</li><li>ByteTrack</li></ul></div></div>
                <div class="pipeline-detail" id="pipeline-step-5"><p><strong>Phase and action recognition.</strong> A temporal model combines recent frames to recognize the phase of the operation, such as dissection, and the action under way, such as retracting tissue.</p><div class="pipeline-models"><span>Example models</span><ul><li>TCN</li><li>LSTM</li><li>Transformer</li></ul></div></div>
                <div class="pipeline-detail" id="pipeline-step-6"><p><strong>Human review.</strong> A clinician confirms or corrects each result. Corrections become new training labels, so the models can keep improving.</p><div class="pipeline-models"><span>Example methods</span><ul><li>Human in the loop</li><li>Active learning</li></ul></div></div>
              </div>
              <p class="figure-note">One frame in slow motion. A stylized scene, not real patient data or model output.</p>
